From 31de493bc2dd4ff2a48c15d60c32537205e9959a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 10:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Carry every QP-C54 tranche beside the adopted catalog rows
 (candidate v2)

Append nine keys to cbz/quarantine/catalog.json, after reconciled_utc:
- proposed_quarantines: 239 main and Math- new records (tranches 1-5 and 8).
- proposed_quarantines_federation: 8 tranche-6 rows from repositories outside the
  catalog's mathematical scope.
- proposed_pinning_amendments: 29 rows that bind their bytes into adopted records already
  holding their claims.
- proposed_byte_pins: 41; 38 are subsumed by an amendment.
- proposed_closed_candidates: 29, the C291 own-receipt group and the 28 P15 declarations.
- held_by_other_lane: 1.
- a3_advice.
- accounting_dispositions: 515 objects or items needing no record, each with its reason,
  including tranche 7's archive members.
- proposal_provenance.

Corrections from different-family checks and from two same-family adversarial review
rounds are applied as errata, field by field; every touched row records errata_applied.
claim_overlaps entries, typed by relation, name records and CLOSED declarations that hold
part of a row's claim. Main is primary where a federation row shares Git blobs with a main
row.

The staging bytes up to the closing brace are unchanged. quarantines, counts, status and
adoption_scope are untouched, so nothing is adopted and no existing record changes. Every
proposal is PROPOSED, owner none and maintenance zero. Adopting any row is a separate
composer decision. Scientific effect NONE.

