+          "line_start": 36,
+          "line_end": 42,
+          "text": "**Theorem G.** For every `ρ ∈ (0, L/4]` and every integer `N ≥ 1` there is `C = C(d, L, ρ, N) < ∞` such that\n\n    ν_eld^{far,ρ}(ℓ) ≤ C ℓ^N,        0 < ℓ ≤ 1.                                                    (0.2)\n\nConsequently, for `0 < t ≤ 1`, `E N_eld^{far,ρ}(0, t] ≤ C t^{N+1}/(N+1)` per unit volume, and for every real `q`\n(however negative) `E Σ_{far elder bars, ℓ_i ≤ t} ℓ_i^q < ∞`: the far elder population has all inverse-lifetime\nmoments."
+        },
+        {
+          "line_start": 46,
+          "line_end": 54,
+          "text": "**Lemma 1 (flat components).** Let `f ∈ C²(X)` and `K > 0` with `K ≥ sup_X ‖D²f‖_op`. Let `x_0` be a local maximum,\n`b = f(x_0)`, and let `t < b` be such that the connected component `C_t` of `x_0` in the open set `{f > t}`\ncontains no point with `f > b`. Then for every `p ∈ C_t`\n\n    |∇f(p)|² ≤ 2K (b − f(p)) ≤ 2K (b − t).                                                          (1.1)\n\nThe hypothesis holds exactly for `t ≥ b − ℓ(x_0)`, where `ℓ(x_0)` is the lifetime of the `H_0` bar of `x_0` under\nthe superlevel filtration with the elder rule ([P] §8): as long as the bar is alive, its component contains no\nolder (higher) maximum, and a component with a point above `b` would contain one (§1)."
+        },
+        {
+          "line_start": 56,
+          "line_end": 58,
+          "text": "**Lemma 2 (crossing).** If the death partner `y` of `x_0` satisfies `dist(x_0, y) ≥ ρ`, then for `t = b − ℓ(x_0)`\nthe component `C_t` meets every sphere `∂B(x_0, r)`, `0 < r < ρ`, and on `C_t` one has `b − ℓ(x_0) < f ≤ b` and\n`|∇f| < (2Kℓ(x_0))^{1/2}`."
+        },
+        {
+          "line_start": 60,
+          "line_end": 61,
+          "text": "**Lemma 3 (near-critical balls).** If `|∇f(p)| ≤ (2K_0ℓ)^{1/2}`, `b − ℓ < f(p) ≤ b`, `sup‖D²f‖ ≤ K_0` and\n`r_ℓ = (ℓ/K_0)^{1/2}`, then every `q ∈ B(p, r_ℓ)` satisfies `|∇f(q)| ≤ 3(K_0ℓ)^{1/2}` and `|f(q) − b| ≤ 3ℓ`."
+        },
+        {
+          "line_start": 276,
+          "line_end": 279,
+          "text": "   - (c) *Consequence for the constant in (0.2).* Suppose (b)'s (2.4) holds for the density (0.1). Then for every `N ≥ 1`\n     there are `c_N > 0` and `ρ_N > 0` such that every constant admissible in (0.2) satisfies\n\n         C(d, L, ρ, N) ≥ c_N ρ^{1−4N},      0 < ρ ≤ ρ_N.                                                  (R6.1)"
