+      "layer_a_status": "A7: source-only evidence with exact finite algebra controls; no kernel declaration. A3 is not engaged by the packet script; the floating-point and Monte Carlo values in the note are explicitly exploration and carry no certification. A2 caution: the result rests on consumed author-side candidate packets.",
+      "exact_boundary": "The source states, for the torus field of #237 §0 in every d ≥ 2 and every L, that |𝐄(k, u)| ≤ C min(k, 1/k) and ν_cand(ℓ) = cℓ^{−1/3} + B_{d,L} + I^{cand}ℓ^{1/4} + c₂ℓ^{1/3} + c₃ℓ^{2/3} + o(ℓ^{2/3}) with c₃ given by (C3) (Theorem C3, lines 139-143), built on Lemma F₃ (the fold-layer limit, lines 132-134) and Lemma T₁ (the cusp tail and a₁ = (1/10)∫F₀db, lines 136-137); for the model kernel e^{−|z|²/2} on R^d, that c₃ = (J/30)∫∫F₀ with J > 0 given by (G), so the model value is positive (Proposition G and Corollary G′, lines 145-160); and that c₃(L) tends to the model value as L → ∞, hence c₃(L) > 0 for L ≥ L₀(d) with L₀(d) unquantified (Proposition G″, lines 162-165). These rest on note LU's Theorem U⁼ and Theorem P⁺ decomposition and on #237, #218, #229 (W⁺.2) and #242, author-side candidates of the same lane. No literal Lean kernel declaration states any of these at this cut; the prose proofs and the exact finite controls are not admitted as closure. Open or conditional steps named by the source: no rate for the o(ℓ^{2/3}) remainder; #242's Conjecture 7 and its inputs (i)-(ii) remain open; L₀(d) is unquantified and nothing is proved at L = 24 (no modulus of continuity for c₃); all numerical values are exploration.",
