+          "text": "5. **The bad-event and schedule comparisons close the relative error.** The cubical bound and (6) give `C(h^(-2)+1) exp(−cT_h²)` without count/event independence. Put `q_h=h²√log(1/h)`. The hypothesis `q_h=o(τ_h)` gives `d_h=o(τ_h)` for fixed A. The two good-event relative terms are `O(d_h/τ_h)=o(1)` and `O(d_h/τ_h^(2/3))=o(1)`. Eventually `τ_h≥q_h`; taking the smaller tail exponent c, a sufficient fixed choice is **`cA²>10/3`**. The bad-event ratio is then bounded by `C h^(cA²−10/3) log(1/h)^(-1/3)=o(1)`. The expectation-ratio conclusion follows by the triangle inequality."
