+          "file": "docs/manuscript/side24_v3_draft_20261013/s2_results.tex",
+          "line_start": 3,
+          "line_end": 8,
+          "text": "\\begin{theorem}[fixed-side short-lifetime law]\\label{thm:main}\nFor the normalized side-24 field \\eqref{eq:K24}, the finite nonessential superlevel $H_0$ first-moment lifetime density satisfies\n\\begin{equation}\\tag{2.1}\\label{eq:main}\n\\nu_{3,24}(\\ell)=c_{3,24}\\,\\ell^{-1/3}\\bigl(1+O(\\ell^{1/3})\\bigr),\\qquad \\ell\\downarrow0,\n\\end{equation}\nequivalently $\\nu_{3,24}(\\ell)=c_{3,24}\\ell^{-1/3}+O(1)$, where $0<c_{3,24}<\\infty$ is given by \\eqref{eq:c} below."
+        },
+        {
+          "file": "docs/manuscript/side24_v3_draft_20261013/s2_results.tex",
+          "line_start": 36,
+          "line_end": 39,
+          "text": "Then\n\\begin{equation}\\tag{2.9}\\label{eq:c}\nc_{3,24}=B_3\\int_{S^2}\\frac{(\\sigma_t^2)^{2/3}D_t}{\\sqrt{\\det\\Sigma_g(t)\\det\\Sigma_h(t)}}\\,dt,\\qquad B_3=\\frac{3\\,\\Gamma(7/6)}{2^{4/3}\\pi^{7/2}} .\n\\end{equation}"
+        },
+        {
+          "file": "docs/manuscript/side24_v3_draft_20261013/s2_results.tex",
+          "line_start": 42,
+          "line_end": 52,
+          "text": "Moreover,\n\\begin{equation}\\tag{2.10}\\label{eq:correction}\n\\frac{c_{3,24}}{c_{3,\\infty}}-1=-\\frac{620813376}{35}\\,e^{-288}+\\varepsilon_{24},\\qquad |\\varepsilon_{24}|<10^{-216},\n\\end{equation}\nwhere $c_{3,\\infty}$, the value of \\eqref{eq:c} for the Bargmann--Fock field on $\\R^3$, is\n\\begin{equation}\\tag{2.11}\\label{eq:cinf}\n\\begin{aligned}\nc_{3,\\infty}&=2^{-23/6}3^{-8/3}(29\\sqrt6-36)\\,\\Gamma(1/6)\\,\\pi^{-5/2}\\\\\n&=0.0417759318405983433429366654285755564666815196\\ldots .\n\\end{aligned}\n\\end{equation}"
+        },
+        {
+          "file": "docs/manuscript/side24_v3_draft_20261013/s2_results.tex",
+          "line_start": 55,
+          "line_end": 59,
+          "text": "In particular $c_{3,24}<c_{3,\\infty}$:\n\\[\n\\frac{c_{3,24}}{c_{3,\\infty}}-1=-1.48621702906582760722\\ldots\\cdot10^{-118}+\\varepsilon_{24},\n\\]\nso the displayed correction is the exact leading term to a relative precision better than $10^{-98}$."
