+          "file": "docs/manuscript/side24_v3_draft_20261013/s1_field.tex",
+          "line_start": 9,
+          "line_end": 11,
+          "text": "\\begin{proposition}[genericity of the side-24 field]\\label{prop:generic}\nThe field $f_{24}$ has real-analytic sample paths and, with probability one, is Morse and has pairwise distinct critical values.\n\\end{proposition}"
+        },
+        {
+          "file": "docs/manuscript/side24_v3_draft_20261013/s1_field.tex",
+          "line_start": 54,
+          "line_end": 60,
+          "text": "\\begin{proposition}[existence of the first-moment lifetime density]\\label{prop:density}\nLet $M_*$ be the global maximum and let $D_f(M)$ be the elder-rule death saddle of a non-global maximum $M$. The finite measure\n\\begin{equation}\\tag{1.9}\\label{eq:Lambda}\n\\Lambda_{3,24}(A)=24^{-3}\\,\\E\\sum_{M\\ne M_*}\\ind_{\\{f_{24}(M)-f_{24}(D_f(M))\\in A\\}},\\qquad A\\subset(0,\\infty),\n\\end{equation}\nis absolutely continuous with respect to Lebesgue measure.\n\\end{proposition}"
+        },
+        {
+          "file": "docs/manuscript/side24_v3_draft_20261013/s3_proof.tex",
+          "line_start": 108,
+          "line_end": 114,
+          "text": "\\begin{lemma}[trichotomy; Supplement Lemma S5.7]\\label{lem:trichotomy}\nOn the Morse event, for an ordered typed pair $(M,S)$ at distance $r$ with midpoint $x$,\n\\[\nA_r\\cap E_r^c\\subset B_r\\cup L_{\\mathrm{same},r},\n\\]\nwhere $A_r$ is gradient adjacency, $E_r=\\{e=1\\}$, $L_{\\mathrm{same},r}$ is same-maximum self-attachment (both ascending half-branches of $S$ end at $M$), and $B_r$ is the existence of a third critical point with value in the pair window $[h,b]$ in one of three spatial regions measured from $x$: the collar $\\{|y-x|\\le C_1r\\}$, the singular-near region $\\{C_1r<|y-x|\\le\\delta\\}$, or at fixed distance $\\{|y-x|>\\delta\\}$. If the two upper sectors of $S$ lie in one component of $\\{f>h\\}$ and not both half-branches end at $M$, that component contains a critical point other than $M$ and $S$ with value in $(h,b)$ (Supplement Lemma S5.7, Case~0, with the merge-level Lemma S5.6), so that case lies in $B_r$. When $M$ is the older birth maximum but $e=0$, the witness is the younger component's own birth maximum $M_2$, with $h<f(M_2)<f(M)$.\n\\end{lemma}"
+        },
+        {
+          "file": "docs/manuscript/side24_v3_draft_20261013/s3_proof.tex",
+          "line_start": 116,
+          "line_end": 125,
+          "text": "\\begin{corollary}[the selection loss has exact order $r^3$]\\label{cor:selection}\nUniformly for $t\\in S^2$ and compact $b,\\kappa>0$,\n\\begin{equation}\\tag{3.13}\\label{eq:selection}\n1-p_r(t,b,\\kappa)\\le Cr^3,\n\\end{equation}\nand, for constants $c,r_*>0$ depending on the compact mark set,\n\\begin{equation}\\tag{3.13a}\\label{eq:selection-lower}\n1-p_r(t,b,\\kappa)\\ge c\\,r^3,\\qquad 0<r\\le r_* .\n\\end{equation}\n\\end{corollary}"
+        },
+        {
+          "file": "docs/manuscript/side24_v3_draft_20261013/s3_proof.tex",
+          "line_start": 145,
+          "line_end": 148,
+          "text": "Second, complete positive Fourier support of \\eqref{eq:K24} implies strict covariance positivity for every linearly independent finite family of derivative-evaluation distributions. Compactness then gives uniform eigenvalue floors for the corrected pair pins joined to a fixed-distance remote value-gradient block. The endpoint determinant factor $r^2$, the remote value window of width $\\kappa r^3/6$ and the Palm normalizer $Z_r\\asymp r^2$ give, uniformly for $t\\in S^2$ and compact $b,\\kappa>0$,\n\\begin{equation}\\tag{3.17}\n\\E_r^{MS}N_{\\rm far}\\le Cr^3 .\n\\end{equation}"
+        },
+        {
+          "file": "docs/manuscript/side24_v3_draft_20261013/s3_proof.tex",
+          "line_start": 304,
+          "line_end": 306,
+          "text": "\\begin{proposition}[bounded remainder]\\label{prop:rate}\nThere are $C,\\ell_*>0$ such that $|\\nu_{3,24}(\\ell)-c_{3,24}\\ell^{-1/3}|\\le C$ for $0<\\ell\\le\\ell_*$.\n\\end{proposition}"
+        }
