+          "file": "docs/manuscript/side24_v3_supplement_draft_20261013/supp_s1_setting.tex",
+          "line_start": 62,
+          "line_end": 66,
+          "text": "\\begin{theorem}[full-spectrum Gram positivity]\\label{thm:setting-gram}\nLet $\\Lambda_1,\\dots,\\Lambda_N$ be finite-order constant-coefficient derivative-evaluation functionals on $\\T^3_{24}$, $\\Lambda_i(f)=(P_i(\\partial)f)(x_i)$ with polynomial symbols $P_i$, and let $\\mathcal T_i=P_i(-\\partial)\\delta_{x_i}$ be the associated distributions, $\\langle\\mathcal T_i,\\varphi\\rangle=\\Lambda_i(\\varphi)$. The covariance matrix $\\bigl(\\Cov(\\Lambda_if,\\Lambda_jf)\\bigr)_{i,j\\le N}$ is positive definite if and only if $\\mathcal T_1,\\dots,\\mathcal T_N$ are linearly independent.\n\nIn particular, if at each of the distinct support points the polynomial symbols of the differential operators evaluated there are linearly independent, then the covariance matrix is positive definite.\n\\end{theorem}"
+        },
