+          "file": "experiments/zeta_fold_exploration/README.md",
+          "line_start": 492,
+          "line_end": 496,
+          "text": "3. *Consequence for H_t.* Folds of H_t occur only at t₀ ≤ Λ, since for t > Λ all zeros are\n   simple [CSV 1994, Corollary 2, p. 114; primary, via review 5486879914]. Conversely, if\n   Λ > 0 then H_Λ has a multiple real zero at finite height. That is a deduction from\n   Polymath15 Theorem 1.5(i), not from the fold, and the zero need not be a nondegenerate double\n   zero (`CLAIMS.md` 6.2). It is not an RH result."
