+          "line_start": 551,
+          "line_end": 554,
+          "text": "   continuity of w'), not O(r²). *Counterexample* (review 5486843735; `test_exact.py`): for\n   H = x² − 2t, a = √(2t), r = 2a and the fixed positive C¹ weight w = 1 + |x|^{1+η} with\n   0 < η < 1, ℓ = 4a³/3 and ℓ_w/ℓ = 1 + 3a^{1+η}/((2+η)(4+η)). For η = ½ this is\n   1 + (4/15)a^{3/2}. On a fixed interval containing the window, both are actual bars for"
