+      "exact_boundary": "Candidate scope: the six files at these blobs:\n- e437045b... (SourceLifetimeAxiomAudit)\n- de65503c... (SourceLifetimeControls)\n- a07036a1... (SourceLifetimeField)\n- e83eb8e1... (SourceLifetimeGeometry)\n- 06d14bc9... (SourceThetaBridge)\n- f2508f7f... (inputs/Lifetime)\n\nThe scope covers the def I4LifetimeField.actualGaussianFieldInterface d L hL : UniversalLaw.Spec.Lifetime.GaussianFieldInterface d L, for all d : ℕ and L > 0, with its supporting theorems:\n- the theta bridge: thetaSum_eq_scaled_cos, sourceSpectralKernel_eq_periodicCovariance and theta_summable;\n- the geometry transport: smoothness, periodicity, Gaussian law, zero means and spectral covariance;\n- the field-level covariance, variance and law identities;\n- the controls.\n\nThe evidence boundary has four parts:\n(a) The receipts are the author's local runs, exported as path projections. They are not CBZ-indexed.\n(b) The kernel evidence is a named-module leanchecker replay, without --fresh, over imports loaded from pre-built .oleans. In this package the 13 imported source modules and Lifetime.lean have compile receipts only. The dependency objects (Mathlib and the rest) were rehashed, not rebuilt.\n(c) Lifetime.lean is a target transcription whose alignment with the source prose is recorded as PENDING_INDEPENDENT_REVIEW. Its original is specifications/lean_statements_20261010/Specifications/Lifetime.lean.\n(d) The 13 inputs are vendored copies of frontiers/source_smooth_realization_20261011 and are outside this candidate.\n\nAlso outside the boundary: Morse genericity, critical-point and persistence measures, elder pairing, the lifetime-density exponent, and every Prop shape in Lifetime.lean (Theorems A/B/C, R1, E2, E4, E11). None of these is asserted.",
