+      "source_hypotheses": "The constructor and the main theorems take only d : ℕ (d = 0 included) and hL : 0 < L. covQuadForm_nonneg and the linear-combination results quantify over every m : ℕ (m = 0 included), every x : Fin m → E d and every a : Fin m → ℝ.\n\nThe interface's fields (Lifetime.lean:150-179) are:\n- the carrier and its sigma-algebra;\n- a probability measure P;\n- the field F;\n- every-sample smoothness IsSmooth (C^n for all finite n);\n- L-periodicity;\n- theta summability;\n- quadratic-form nonnegativity;\n- the exact centred Gaussian law of every finite linear combination;\n- the raw product covariance E[F x F y] = periodicCovariance d L (x - y).\n\nThe constructor supplies the existing SmoothSample d L carrier and smoothLaw d L, and as the field, smoothSourceField d L composed with the canonical Euclidean equivalence. The imported facts it relies on include smoothLaw_isProbabilityMeasure, smoothSourceField_contDiff, I4Lattice.sourceField_lattice_shift, smoothSourceField_finiteVector_hasGaussianLaw, observation_map_eq, I4SourceGaussian.source_linearCombination_hasGaussianLaw, I4SourceCovariance.sourceField_integral_zero, smoothSourceField_covariance, finite_product_summable and Mathlib's Complex.tsum_exp_neg_quadratic.",
+      "source_dependencies": "Import graph:\n- SourceLifetimeField imports SourceLifetimeGeometry and SourceThetaBridge.\n- SourceLifetimeGeometry imports Lifetime and SourceSmoothCarrier.\n- SourceThetaBridge imports Lifetime, SourceKernel and Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Gaussian.PoissonSummation.\n- SourceLifetimeControls imports SourceLifetimeField.\n- SourceLifetimeAxiomAudit imports SourceLifetimeField, SourceLifetimeControls, SourceSmoothControls, Lean.Elab.Command and Lean.Util.CollectAxioms.\n- inputs/Lifetime imports Mathlib.\n\nThe 13 other inputs/ modules are needed transitively: GaussianSeriesFoundation, SpectralWeights, SourceFourierSeries, SourceLattice, SourceKernel, SourceGaussianLaw, SourceCovariance, SourceC4, SourceSmooth, SourceTorus, SourceTorusC4, SourceSmoothCarrier and SourceSmoothControls. Per PROVENANCE.md they are byte copies of frontiers/source_smooth_realization_20261011/ at Math- commit 57ddbd6b..., and their content at the cut matches the files at that path (for example SourceKernel, blob 5d5602ac...). They are not part of this record, and their CBZ status is not assessed here.\n\nMathlib rev d13f23b723b8a846827a245b89c10fc7d3f11612.\n\nDownstream consumer: frontiers/compact_morse_elder_adapter_20261018/inputs/C291 vendors SourceLifetimeField.lean, SourceLifetimeGeometry.lean and inputs/Lifetime.lean.",
+      "source_self_limits": "README line 5: the kernel checks did not use --fresh, and the dependencies were not rebuilt from source.\n\nREADME line 33: 'lake build' 'has not been executed' in the original delivery. The hosted gate status is NOT_REGISTERED_NOT_CLAIMED, and the package adds no workflow.\n\nREADME line 39: the package does not:\n- construct critical-point or persistence-bar measures;\n- prove Morse genericity;\n- identify elder pairing with branch adjacency;\n- convert contact integrals into once-counted bars;\n- prove an all-small-bars converse;\n- close the regional collision bound.\nThe lifetime-density exponent, short-bar law and universality conclusions 'do not follow from this package alone', and no scientific register is promoted.\n\nREADME line 41: the nonauthor review (OpenAI Codex) is by the same provider and session lineage, with independence credit 0 and scientific effect NONE.\n\nREADME line 43: the package is delegated AI work. No human or provider-distinct review is claimed.\n\nCorrection of 24 Oct 2026 (README lines 45-95):\n- Lines 47-53 say the earlier text describes the 18 October delivery, and they cite a later external Claude S reproduction (PR 477 comment 6245744181) that reports a successful ordinary lake build from independently built pinned dependencies.\n- PASS_STATIC_ONLY and PASS_SOURCE_STATIC_ONLY do not certify the theorem or the cache.\n- Line 92: the repair's fixtures 'do not constitute a new lake build reproduction or hosted Lean run'.\n\nLifetime.lean header (lines 7-48): scientific effect NONE, statements only, 'no kernel receipt about them exists', and alignment PENDING_INDEPENDENT_REVIEW.\n\nNEXT_TASK.md: including dimension zero does not extend downstream theorems to that dimension.",
+      "finite_checks": "There are no numeric checks. The Lean controls in SourceLifetimeControls.lean cover degenerate and finite families:\n- dimension-zero theta = 1;\n- spectral normalizer = 1;\n- raw variance = 1;\n- empty-family law = dirac 0;\n- cancelled pair [x, x] with coefficients [1, -1]: law = dirac 0;\n- reinforced pair: quadratic form = 4, law gaussianReal 0 4;\n- Euclidean norm squared of (1, 1) = 2;\n- shifted field mean = 1.\n\nREADME line 9 and the evidence/final/negative-project and negative-runs records report three further checks. Seven source mutations were rejected. An unused-custom-axiom fixture was rejected by the audit. A binding probe printed 21 helper references. The baseline's original control_pass false is preserved.\n\nThe README also reports two verifier counts. verify_execution.py (original sha256 85a80984...) passed 579 checks, and verify_mutations.py (8d9ec220...) passed 265, per REVIEW_C291_ACTUAL_FINAL_EXECUTION_VERIFICATION.json and REVIEW_C291_ACTUAL_MUTATION_VERIFICATION.json.\n\nNone of these was run here.",
+      "floating_point": "NONE. The group contains Python: validate_static.py, test_static_validator.py, evidence/history/scaffold-17modules/validate_static.py, and the evidence/final/*.py runner, rehash, verify and export scripts plus the RUNNER.py files.\n\nA grep found no float type use, numpy, mpmath, math module, fractions or decimal in them. Floating point appears only in wall-clock timing: run_final_phase.py, run_kernel_recovery_phase.py, run_recovery_phase.py and the negative-runs RUNNER.py and IMPORTED_RUNNER.py files compute elapsed seconds with time.monotonic(). That timing bears on no claim.\n\nThe scripts hash, orchestrate and check records; none computes or certifies a numeric bound. The README states that PASS_STATIC_ONLY 'does not execute Lean or certify the theorem'. The Lean files use exact ℝ and ℂ, with no Float.",
