+      "reason": "This is a byte-identity inventory of the owner's Dropbox Github/ subtree compared with Git blobs and two archives, plus the scripts that built it. README.md:3 reads 'Scientific effect NONE. This directory is an inventory of byte identity ... It moves no status, edits no ledger'. README.md:51 says byte identity 'says nothing about which copy is canonical, nor about correctness', and README.md:55 says 'Nothing here is a scientific result or a status change'. PINS.json:1-46 holds the digests and row counts of the local inputs and, at :41-45, the ledger commit. The top-level keys of SUMMARY.json are tier, folder and ledger-hit counts, byte totals, aggregation rules and a hash receipt. The own/ scripts merge pages, classify by name, size and hash, batch and harvest hashes, name-match ledger rows, index zip members, assemble the directory and write the README (own/merge.py:2, own/classify_ns.py:2-3, own/classify_hash.py:2-7, own/ledger_crosswalk.py:2-8, own/zip_index.py:2, own/build_pr.py:2-10, own/readme_gen.py:2). None of these files makes a mathematical claim.",
