+      "title": "Successor review-notes catalog/routing indexes (v5-v7, v9-v92)",
+      "reason": "Each of these 87 files is a short successor catalog and routing index with no mathematical content of its own.\n\nStructure (checked in all 87 files):\n- Line 3 begins 'Supersedes', names the previous index key and reads 'Scientific effect: NONE.' INDEX_v5.md:3 has 'Supersedes catalog key `review-notes-index-v4` without mutating its bytes'. Every other file has 'Supersedes `review-notes-index-vN`.' Some line-3s add a CI bound, for example INDEX_v14.md:3 'Catalog at CI bound 128'.\n- A table of catalog key / surface / role starts at line 5 and ends between line 9 and line 16 (for example INDEX_v14.md:5-9, INDEX_v5.md:5-16, INDEX_v79.md:5-16). Each row names one catalogued key, or is a 'prior keys ... Frozen' row.\n- The last line is a coordination line:\n  - 60 files begin it with 'Next:': INDEX_v9.md:14, INDEX_v33.md:11, and INDEX_v35.md through INDEX_v92.md (for example INDEX_v92.md:13).\n  - 22 files begin it with '`#90` still OPEN': INDEX_v12.md through INDEX_v32.md and INDEX_v34.md (for example INDEX_v17.md:12, INDEX_v22.md:11).\n  - The other five are INDEX_v5.md:18 'Unclaimed:', INDEX_v6.md:14 'Next meta focus after this:', INDEX_v7.md:14 'Await', INDEX_v10.md:15 'Priority reviews:' and INDEX_v11.md:14 'Priority:'.\n\nThe roles are engineering, coordination or status labels. Examples:\n- INDEX_v6.md:10 'replay FAILURE; #90 still blocked'\n- INDEX_v14.md:3 'Catalog at CI bound 128'\n- INDEX_v35.md:7 'Eng-gate close + merge `ebedb780`; not theorem ACCEPT'\n- INDEX_v46.md:7 'V3.4/arithmetic_ledgers custody note-only'\n- INDEX_v79.md:7-13, main PR168-175 'note-only'\n- INDEX_v92.md:7 'required formal gate package'\n\nSome rows name a mathematical package, ledger, custody import, erratum or tip catalogued elsewhere. These are bare topic labels pointing at separately catalogued objects. They restate no statement, bound, constant, formula or certificate. They include:\n- INDEX_v5.md:10-11 and :14\n- INDEX_v6.md:8-9\n- INDEX_v7.md:8\n- INDEX_v9.md:11\n- INDEX_v10.md:9 and :11\n- INDEX_v11.md:9 and :11\n- INDEX_v12.md:7 and INDEX_v13.md:10 (merged PR15 transition gate package)\n- INDEX_v13.md:7-8\n- INDEX_v16.md:7-9\n- INDEX_v17.md:9\n- INDEX_v20.md:7-9\n- INDEX_v26.md:7-9 and :11\n- INDEX_v28.md:7\n- INDEX_v29.md:7 and :9\n- INDEX_v35.md:8-10\n- INDEX_v37.md:7-8\n- INDEX_v52.md:7-9\n- INDEX_v53.md:7 (PROOF_INDEX nav note)\n- INDEX_v59.md:7 (SIDE24 chart intake note-only)\n- INDEX_v64.md:7-9\n- INDEX_v65.md:7-9\n- INDEX_v66.md:7-10 ('Hessian congruence erratum', 'P15 ASCII 3E−2 note')\n- INDEX_v68.md:7\n- INDEX_v69.md:7-8\n- INDEX_v71.md:7-8\n- INDEX_v72.md:7\n- INDEX_v74.md:7 (LB-RATE HOLD note-only)\n- INDEX_v77.md:8 (noncertifying/float-labelling note-only)\n- INDEX_v79.md:8 and :10 (H3 interval, H3-RUNG-FLOOR note-only)\n- INDEX_v82.md:7\n- INDEX_v84.md:7\n- INDEX_v85.md:7\n- INDEX_v88.md:7-8\n- INDEX_v89.md:7 and :9\n- INDEX_v90.md:7-8\n- INDEX_v91.md:7\n- INDEX_v92.md:7\n- the 'Merge note' rows that go with these packages (for example INDEX_v66.md:11-12, INDEX_v71.md:9, INDEX_v72.md:8, INDEX_v88.md:9, INDEX_v90.md:9)\nAny obligation belongs to those objects themselves.\n\nRows that mention acceptance only report outside status and say so:\n- INDEX_v30.md:8 'PR4 merge coordination (not math ACCEPT)'\n- INDEX_v35.md:7 'not theorem ACCEPT'\n- INDEX_v35.md:8 'Coordination note for P15 nonauthor ACCEPT' points at the catalogued note `math-pr63-p15-full-price-accept` for Math- merge `1e1114f5`. The index records no acceptance of its own.\n\nRows that say 'density still open', 'pin AMEND still open' or similar only report open status: INDEX_v5.md:14, INDEX_v6.md:9, INDEX_v9.md:11, INDEX_v10.md:11, INDEX_v11.md:11 and INDEX_v13.md:8.\n\nregistry.json:5972 records the registry's top-level 'scientific_status_authority': false.",
