+      "classification": "NOT_OBLIGATION",
+      "title": "Meta-framework catalog/custody/tip receipts for Math- PRs (identity tables and status notes only)",
+      "reason": "These 33 MATH_*.md files are meta-framework catalog, custody and tip receipts for Math- PRs. Each has a 'Scientific effect: NONE' line (e.g. MATH_PR89_BF_SIX_PIN_MERGED.md:6, MATH_PR64_ERRATUM_MERGED.md:6, MATH_D5_LANDING_20260926.md:4, MATH_PR15_GREEN.md:8). MATH_PR66_LANDING_REVIEWED_SCOPED.md:6 has 'NONE from meta-framework'. Most hold key/path/bytes/SHA256 tables of Math- paths (e.g. MATH_PR89_BF_SIX_PIN_MERGED.md:12-38, MATH_PR87_CYCLE4_HARPER_MERGED.md:10-23, MATH_PR82_D5_MICRODISK_MERGED.md:10-13), plus non-claims (MATH_PR89_BF_SIX_PIN_MERGED.md:48-49: 'No mathematical review'; 'Does not promote AUTHOR_DERIVATION certificates to prize acceptance'). MATH_PR66:17-20 and MATH_PR79:12-14 table meta-framework replica paths rather than Math- paths. The six notes MATH_PR15_GREEN, MATH_PR15_MERGED, MATH_PR15_REPLAY_STATUS, MATH_PR15_TIP_8C4C946A, MATH_PR15_TRANSITION and MATH_PR78_VAULT_SECURITY_MERGED.md record tip, CI or merge status without path tables; MATH_PR15_GREEN:6 and MATH_PR15_MERGED:15 cite only a CI artifact SHA256. MATH_D5_LANDING_20260926.md:8-13 is a PR/head/merge/package-directory table with no bytes or SHA256. The mathematical packets these notes index live in Math- at the named paths. Among them: the BF six-pin scalar/Hessian packages (MATH_PR89:18-38); the lifetime-parent files ERRATUM_CONGRUENCE.md (MATH_PR64:12), UNIFORM_MATRIX_CAP_AND_LIFETIME.md and MARKED_CYLINDER_CAP_PROOF.md (MATH_PR50_PR51:19-20) and CAP_PAIRING_IDENTITIES.md (MATH_PR85:13); the P15 PROOF.md with its nonauthor REVIEW.md and algebra_check.py (MATH_PR63:12-22); TRANSVERSE_BOUND_CANDIDATE.md (MATH_PR54:13); the D5 microdisk NOTE and QUARTIC (MATH_PR82:12-13); the cycle-4 Harper packet (MATH_PR87:12-23); the pin-neighborhood recon (MATH_PR53:12-13); the H5 rim-contract repair (MATH_PR86:12-17); the drive-hole ledger (MATH_PR81:12); the transverse-contact import and companions (MATH_PR94:12-15, MATH_PR95:12-20); and the contact-kernel substitute (MATH_PR80:12-13). The notes quote none of those packets' statements. MATH_PR64_ERRATUM_MERGED.md:12 records only the key, path, bytes and SHA256 of `imports/lifetime_parent_20260925/ERRATUM_CONGRUENCE.md`, and :6 says 'Additive erratum only; original parent bytes unchanged; does not accept Theorem A'. MATH_PR82_D5_MICRODISK_MERGED.md:6 lists only non-claims ('Does not claim all-height $O(r^3)$ pin-neighborhood expected count ...'). MATH_PR53_PIN_NEIGHBORHOOD_MERGED.md:18 describes the packet's scope ('Outer-cone/steep-strip `O(r^3)` reconnaissance only') and reports 'punctured-disk bound withdrawn' without stating any bound. MATH_PR85_CUSTODY_NOTES_MERGED.md:20 says the indexed pairing identities 'remain conditional on stated embed/Morse hypotheses' without stating them. MATH_PR84:20 and MATH_PR80:18 report custody and provenance status ('Rim exponent mismatch disclosed in packet review — not a scientific promotion'; 'type-mass constants remain non-original to TRANSVERSE source') without stating any exponent or constant. Other notes cover transition-gate, CI, Lean-lane or security engineering. MATH_PR15_TRANSITION.md:10-15 lists four transition-gate holes. MATH_PR76, 79, 92 and 96 cover the workflow display name, action pins, the Lean lane and required checks. MATH_PR78:6 covers SECURITY.md, CODEOWNERS and dependabot.yml only. The batch facts give no copy_of for these files, and they add no mathematics. Side note: the tree at this ref also holds three CI YAML replicas (MATH_DOWNSTREAM_GATE_WORKFLOW_PR79.yml, MATH_DOWNSTREAM_GATE_WORKFLOW_PR96.yml, MATH_FORMAL_LEAN_WORKFLOW_PR96.yml), named at MATH_PR79_ACTIONS_BUMP_MERGED.md:14 and MATH_PR96_REQUIRED_FORMAL_MERGED.md:16-17. They are not in the batch file list, so they are not itemized here.",
