+      "classification": "NOT_OBLIGATION",
+      "title": "Peer coordination refresh notes v13-v91 (tip watches and routing)",
+      "reason": "Each of these 73 PEER_COORDINATION_*.md files has a line 3 beginning '**Scientific effect:** NONE. Meta-framework watch only.' (V13-V50) or '**Scientific effect:** NONE. Catalog/routing only.' (V51-V91). V13, V14, V21, V26, V64 and V66 add catalog-room, CI-bound or 'no new merges' text on that line. Each file is a table of PR tips and merge states with one-line reads (e.g. PEER_COORDINATION_20260925_V13.md:5-17; PEER_COORDINATION_20260926_V91.md:5-10). Most add a routing section: '## Meta-framework posture' (V13-V20, V23), '## Catalog posture' (V21, V22), '## This lane' (V28-V50), or a 'Next:' clause (V52-V91 on its own line; V51:17 inside a paragraph). V24, V26 and V27 have no routing section. Mathematical topics appear only as short labels for other lanes' PRs. For example, PEER_COORDINATION_20260925_V13.md:10 has 'C6 remainder constants + six-pin regression oracle' for Math- PR19, and PEER_COORDINATION_20260925_V17.md:20 has 'Typed contact kernel k^6 small-gap / directional suppression' for Math- PR36. These labels come with explicit instructions not to duplicate or catalog those bodies (PEER_COORDINATION_20260925_V17.md:13 'Math frontier (do not duplicate)'; PEER_COORDINATION_20260925_V13.md:26). The rest is catalog-bound bookkeeping (e.g. PEER_COORDINATION_20260925_V14.md:3, PEER_COORDINATION_20260926_V64.md:3). No mathematical claim is stated.",
