+      "title": "Dispatch records relaying and re-checking cross-model findings on Math- PR9 axial row",
+      "reason": "These 11 dispatch versions are grouped here because each carries either a finding record (v1-v7) or a content-level check of the J_grad_x sample in PR9's axial row (v8-v11). They agree or disagree with named objects and add no new result.\n- MULTI_AGENT_DISPATCH_20260925.json:62-70 records verified_cross_model_finding 'PR9-axial-J_grad_x-deterministic'. Its reporter is 'OpenAI (via #86 ultra-close)' (line 64), its tip is 'Math- PR9 chart package (axial_contact_rows)' (line 66), and its statement (line 67) is that on C_axial the leading J_grad_x = 6 k y1^2 is deterministic, so the axial net r^2 identity is diagnostic until a compensation-density bound exists. Its local_check (line 68) is 'axial_contact_rows returns J_grad_x: 6*k*y1*y1; PROOF.md §4.5 matches'. This is a re-check of PR9's own formula.\n- v2:27-31 and v2:87-91, v3:30-32 and v3:94-98, v4:79-83, v5:62-65 and v6:86-89 re-record that finding's status on later PR9 tips from PR9's RESULTS flags (axial_gaussian_density_factor_bounded=false, contact_density_bound_proved=false).\n- v7:59-71 relays the 'PR9-pin-midpoint-offset' finding. Its reporter is 'OpenAI via Math- PR16/PR17' (line 63), and its statement (line 64) is that the axial row is 6k(y1^2-1/4), not 6k y1^2. That correction is attributed to Math- PR16 and PR17 (v7:39-47, v7:82), not derived here.\n- v7:72-77 relays an engineering finding against main-PR98's claims_gate_adapter, and v5:30-33 records the disposition 'AMEND_REQUIRED (T1,T6,T8)' for governance-PR4.\n- v8:43-46, v9:38-41, v10:48-51 and v11:32-35 re-check whether each new PR9 tip applied the AMEND, and they name the J_grad_x sample shape (v8:45 'axial J_grad_x sample still 6ky1^2 shape', v9:40 'J_grad_x sample still unrepaired 6ky1^2 shape', v10:50, v11:34). Later versions v12-v24 report only that the AMEND was not applied, without naming PR9 row content, and are in the other item.\n- v10:38-43 quotes Math-PR21's claim OA-D5-AXIAL-DENSITY-20260925-CONSENSUS as observed tip