+            "issue": "The two items give inconsistent reasons for the same kind of line. The relay item treats PR9 tip lines in v8, v9 and v11 as re-checks of whether each tip applied the AMEND. The coordination item treats similar PR9 tip lines in v12-v24 as plain state labels: v12:40, v13:44 and v14:64 'pin AMEND unrepaired', and v15:43 through v24:40 'not regenerated from corrected pins'. The difference that actually exists in the files is that v8:45, v9:40, v10:50 and v11:34 name the J_grad_x sample shape of PR9's rows, while v12-v24 report only whether the AMEND was applied. Neither group has mathematics of its own, so no obligation is missed. The partition is kept and both reasons now state this rule."
