+      "reason": "Route indexes and multi-agent dispatch plans: lists of observed PR tips and merge commits, lane assignments, protocol rules and catalog-bound changes.\n- DOWNSTREAM_ROUTE_20260925_v3.json:14-15 has \"scientific_status_authority\": false and 'Exact source identities and review surfaces ... Not a lemma_closed register'. Its layers (D0-D7, lines 47-106) map review issues to catalog keys only. Its line 9 'disposition' is a process disposition of main issue #61 ('SUPERSEDED_NONBLOCKING by #86 — dispatch surface only; mathematical obligations retained on D0–D7'), not a mathematical verdict.\n- MULTI_AGENT_DISPATCH_20260925_v91.json:6-8 records a Math- PR96 merge note, the catalog bound of 600 and 'Scientific effect NONE'. Lines 9-18 are protocol rules.\n- A recursive key scan of all 94 routing files for verified_cross_model_finding, cross_model_findings, statement, local_check and disposition matches v1-v7 and v10, which are in the other item, and, in this item, only that process disposition at DOWNSTREAM_ROUTE_20260925_v3.json:9. Keys named claim (v12:46, v14:43, v16:34, v17:35) hold only claim identifiers such as 'OA-D5-THIN-TUBE-20260925'. Keys named bound or catalog_bound (for example v14:26, v32:39) hold the catalog size cap.\n- Their Math- PR mentions are state labels, for example v13 Math-PR19 'C6 bounds + six-pin regression oracle; replay green' (v13:48) and v25:31 Math-PR9 'CLOSED_UNMERGED'. v12:40 ('tridecic G_*_next enumerated; finite-r pin AMEND still unrepaired'), v13:44 and v14:64 ('pin AMEND unrepaired'), and v15:43 through v24:40 ('not yet regenerated from corrected pins' or 'not regenerated from corrected pins') report whether later PR9 tips applied the AMEND recorded in v7. They do not name PR9's row content or state any formula, which is the difference from v8-v11 in the other item. None of these lines makes a mathematical claim of its own.",
